<DocsLayout title="Configuration" description="RelayCore configuration reference">
  <h1>Configuration</h1>

  <p>Configuration comes from four layers, in this order: <strong>CLI flag &gt; environment variable &gt; config file &gt; built-in default</strong>. A one-off override therefore never requires editing a file, and settings that must survive across commands go in <code>$RELAY_DATA_DIR/config.toml</code>.</p>

  <p><code>relay-core-cli config init</code> writes a commented config file, <code>relay-core-cli config show</code> prints the settings <strong>in effect</strong> (file values merged over the defaults), and <code>relay-core-cli config path</code> prints where the file lives. A config file that cannot be parsed <strong>stops the command</strong> instead of falling back to defaults: silently ignoring a typo runs a daemon with settings nobody asked for.

  <h2>Default data directory</h2>

  <p>The default directory is <code>~/.relay-core</code> (override with <code>RELAY_DATA_DIR</code>). HTTPS interception files:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><code>ca_cert.pem</code> — CA certificate</li>
    <li><code>ca_key.pem</code> — CA private key</li>
    <li><code>ca_cert.json</code> — CA metadata (required for persistent load)</li>
  </ul>

  <p>After <code>relay-core-cli ca generate</code>, the daemon reads from these paths. When the files are missing it creates them on first start; HTTPS interception still needs <code>ca install</code> to trust that CA, plain HTTP does not.</p>

  <p>The same directory also holds <code>daemon.db</code> (SQLite for flows and audit), <code>daemon.json</code> (discovery manifest), and logs. The CLI and MCP share this directory by default; set a different <code>RELAY_DATA_DIR</code> to isolate an experiment, or use <code>relay-core-cli start --in-memory</code>.</p>

  <h2>Flow retention</h2>

  <p>Since 0.13.1 the product default is <strong>at most 5000 flows, and drop anything older than 7 days</strong> (audit events stay unbounded by default). Hot data is an in-memory LRU of about 200 flows; persistence remains SQLite. Use MCP <code>clear_flows</code> or policy <code>retention</code> to purge / retune; an explicitly empty retention means unbounded.</p>

  <h2>Config file</h2>

  <pre><code># ~/.relay-core/config.toml — set only what you change; the rest uses built-in defaults
[daemon]
api_port = 8082        # control API / Web UI port (an ephemeral port is used when taken)
mcp_port = 18083       # MCP endpoint port
mcp = true             # serve the MCP endpoint from the daemon
idle_timeout = 0       # stop the proxy after N seconds without traffic; 0 = never
save_stream = ""       # append every flow update as JSONL here (empty = no recording)

[proxy]
port = 8080            # port `start` / `run` use when none is named

[client]
autostart_daemon = true   # may the MCP bridge start a daemon on its own?

[tui]
# theme = "relay"      # relay | slate | high-contrast (see below)</code></pre>


  <h2>Environment variables</h2>

  <table>
    <tr><th>Variable</th><th>Description</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RELAY_DATA_DIR</code></td><td>Data directory (default <code>~/.relay-core</code>)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RELAY_CA_CERT</code></td><td>CA cert path (must be paired with <code>RELAY_CA_KEY</code>); applies to <code>relay-core-cli</code> and <code>relay-core-probe</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RELAY_CA_KEY</code></td><td>CA key path (must be paired with <code>RELAY_CA_CERT</code>)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RELAY_LOG</code></td><td>Log filter level (e.g. <code>info</code>, <code>debug</code>, <code>trace</code>)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RELAY_CORE_TUI_THEME</code></td><td>TUI color preset when <code>--theme</code> is omitted (<code>relay</code>, <code>slate</code>, <code>high-contrast</code>). See <a href="/en/docs/tui#themes">TUI themes</a>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RELAYCORE_UPSTREAM_PASSWORD</code></td><td>Upstream proxy HTTP Basic auth password. Paired with <code>--upstream-auth-user</code>. Never pass the password via CLI — it would land in shell history. See <a href="/en/docs/proxy-modes#upstream-proxy">Proxy Modes § upstream</a>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RELAY_API_PORT</code> / <code>RELAY_MCP_PORT</code> / <code>RELAY_PROXY_PORT</code></td><td>Port overrides for the daemon and the proxy (<code>--api-port</code> / <code>--mcp-port</code> / <code>--listen</code>)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RELAY_PROXY_IDLE_TIMEOUT</code></td><td>Seconds without captured traffic before the proxy stops; <code>0</code> never stops it</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RELAY_MCP_URL</code> / <code>RELAY_MCP_TOKEN</code></td><td>Point the MCP bridge at an explicit endpoint instead of discovering the daemon</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RELAY_MCP_NO_AUTOSTART</code></td><td>Set to <code>1</code> to forbid the MCP bridge from starting a daemon itself</td></tr>
  </table>

  <p>Path precedence: <strong>CLI args &gt; environment variables &gt; default data directory</strong>.</p>

  <h2>TUI theme</h2>

  <p>The TUI takes its theme from <code>[tui].theme</code> in the file above — one file, one reader, so <code>relay-core-cli config show</code> reports it too. Resolution order: <code>--theme</code> flag &gt; <code>RELAY_CORE_TUI_THEME</code> env &gt; <code>[tui].theme</code> &gt; default (<code>relay</code>).</p>

  <h2>Common CLI flags</h2>

  <pre><code>relay-core-cli start [options]      # daemon + proxy (idempotent)
relay-core-cli run [options]        # the same daemon, in the foreground

  -l/--listen &lt;ADDR&gt;     Proxy listen address (default 127.0.0.1:8080)
  --ca-cert &lt;PATH&gt;       CA certificate path (optional override)
  --ca-key &lt;PATH&gt;        CA private key path (must pair with --ca-cert)
  --api-port &lt;PORT&gt;      Control API / Web UI port (ephemeral when taken)
  --api-token &lt;TOKEN&gt;    Bearer token (the daemon generates one by default)
  --mcp-port &lt;PORT&gt;      Serve the MCP endpoint from the daemon
  --rules &lt;PATH&gt;         Load rules file (JSON/YAML)
  --script &lt;PATH&gt;        Load Deno script
  --script-env-allow      Comma-separated env var names scripts may read
  --ui                   Foreground daemon with the TUI attached as a client
  --theme &lt;NAME&gt;         TUI color preset
  --upstream &lt;URL&gt;       Route all traffic through a parent proxy
  --save-stream &lt;PATH&gt;   Append every flow update as JSONL to disk</code></pre>

  <h2>Production notes</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Bind to <code>127.0.0.1</code> for local-only use</li>
    <li>When using <code>--api-port</code>, protect access with <code>--api-token</code></li>
    <li>For shared team CA, align on <code>RELAY_DATA_DIR</code> or explicit <code>--ca-cert</code> / <code>--ca-key</code></li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
